<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Security Awareness Program</title>

<style>
*{
  box-sizing:border-box;
  margin:0;
  padding:0;
}

body{
  font-family:"Segoe UI",Roboto,Arial,sans-serif;
  background:#eef1f6;
  color:#1f2733;
  min-height:100vh;
  display:flex;
  align-items:flex-start;
  justify-content:center;
  padding:32px 16px;
  overflow-y:auto;
  -webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased;
}

.card{
  width:100%;
  max-width:720px;
  background:#fff;
  border-radius:18px;
  overflow:hidden;
  margin:20px 0;
  box-shadow:
    0 24px 60px -18px rgba(20,40,80,.35),
    0 6px 16px rgba(20,40,80,.10);
}

.top{
  background:#005BAC;
  color:#fff;
  padding:26px 34px;
  display:flex;
  align-items:center;
  gap:16px;
}

.logo{
  width:56px;
  height:56px;
  border-radius:12px;
  background:#fff;
  flex:0 0 auto;
  display:flex;
  align-items:center;
  justify-content:center;
  font-weight:800;
  font-size:22px;
  color:#005BAC;
}

.co{
  font-size:12px;
  font-weight:600;
  line-height:1.4;
}

.co b{
  display:block;
  font-size:15px;
  font-weight:700;
}

.hero{
  padding:30px 34px 6px;
}

.flag{
  display:inline-flex;
  align-items:center;
  gap:8px;
  background:#fdeaea;
  color:#b42318;
  border:1px solid #f4c2c2;
  border-radius:999px;
  padding:6px 14px;
  font-size:12px;
  font-weight:700;
  letter-spacing:.4px;
  margin-bottom:16px;
}

.flag .d{
  width:8px;
  height:8px;
  border-radius:50%;
  background:#e24b4a;
}

h1{
  font-size:30px;
  font-weight:800;
  color:#12233b;
  margin-bottom:10px;
}

.lead{
  font-size:15px;
  line-height:1.6;
  color:#44546a;
}

.body{
  padding:18px 34px 8px;
}

.note{
  background:#f5f8fc;
  border:1px solid #e2eaf3;
  border-radius:12px;
  padding:16px 18px;
  font-size:14px;
  line-height:1.6;
  color:#2c3b4f;
  margin-bottom:22px;
}

.grid{
  display:grid;
  grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;
  gap:12px;
}

.tell{
  border:1px solid #e7ebf0;
  border-radius:12px;
  padding:15px 16px;
  background:#fff;
}

.tell .t{
  display:flex;
  align-items:center;
  gap:9px;
  font-size:14px;
  font-weight:700;
  color:#12233b;
  margin-bottom:5px;
}

.tell .t i{
  width:26px;
  height:26px;
  border-radius:7px;
  background:#e8f1fb;
  color:#005BAC;
  display:flex;
  align-items:center;
  justify-content:center;
  font-style:normal;
  font-weight:800;
}

.tell p{
  font-size:12.5px;
  line-height:1.5;
  color:#5a6b80;
}

.rule{
  margin:22px 0 4px;
  background:#005BAC;
  color:#fff;
  border-radius:12px;
  padding:18px 20px;
}

.rule .k{
  font-size:11px;
  font-weight:700;
  letter-spacing:1.2px;
  margin-bottom:6px;
}

.rule .v{
  font-size:17px;
  font-weight:700;
  line-height:1.4;
}

.foot{
  padding:20px 34px 26px;
  border-top:1px solid #eef1f5;
  margin-top:20px;
  display:flex;
  align-items:center;
  justify-content:space-between;
  gap:16px;
  flex-wrap:wrap;
}

.report{
  font-size:13px;
  color:#44546a;
  line-height:1.5;
}

.ok{
  background:#e9f6ee;
  color:#166534;
  border:1px solid #bfe3cb;
  border-radius:10px;
  padding:10px 16px;
  font-size:13px;
  font-weight:700;
  white-space:nowrap;
}

@media(max-width:560px){
  .grid{
    grid-template-columns:1fr;
  }

  h1{
    font-size:24px;
  }

  .top,
  .hero,
  .body,
  .foot{
    padding-left:20px;
    padding-right:20px;
  }
}
</style>

</head>

<body>

<div class="card">

<div class="top">
  <div class="logo">IT</div>
  <div class="co">
    <b>Security Awareness Program</b>
    Cyber Security Awareness & Training<br>
    Building a safer digital workplace
  </div>
</div>

<div class="hero">

<div class="flag">
<span class="d"></span>
SECURITY AWARENESS DRILL
</div>

<h1>…relax. This was a security-awareness drill.</h1>

<p class="lead">
You just pasted and ran a command you did not write — the exact move behind
a real attack technique called <b>ClickFix</b>. This one was harmless.
A real one would not be.
</p>

</div>


<div class="body">

<div class="note">
In the seconds it took this page to appear, a <b>real</b> ClickFix command
could have silently installed an info-stealer or handed remote control of
this machine to an attacker — with <b>no window, no warning, nothing visible</b>.
And notice: you could not read what you pasted.
<b>That unreadable blob was the red flag.</b>
</div>


<div class="grid">

<div class="tell">
<div class="t"><i>1</i> A page told you to run something</div>
<p>Real verification never asks you to open Run, PowerShell or a terminal. That instruction alone is the attack.</p>
</div>

<div class="tell">
<div class="t"><i>2</i> You couldn't read the command</div>
<p>Long encoded commands and hidden scripts exist to hide intent. Unreadable means dangerous.</p>
</div>

<div class="tell">
<div class="t"><i>3</i> It bypassed safety controls</div>
<p>Security protections should not be disabled to complete a normal verification step.</p>
</div>

<div class="tell">
<div class="t"><i>4</i> It felt urgent</div>
<p>"Fix immediately" or "verification failed" messages create pressure so you act before thinking.</p>
</div>

</div>


<div class="rule">
<div class="k">GOLDEN RULE</div>
<div class="v">
Never paste a command into the Run box, PowerShell or a terminal unless you typed it yourself.
</div>
</div>

</div>


<div class="foot">

<div class="report">
Think you ran something real?
<b>Report it to your security team immediately.</b><br>
Early reporting helps reduce impact.
</div>

<div class="ok">
✓ Demo complete
</div>

</div>

</div>

</body>
</html>